    <string name="ssh_key_title">SSH key</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_intro">WakeDeck logs in to your PC with this key, never with a password. The private key stays in the phone\'s secure storage and cannot be copied out. Add this public key to each PC:</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_copy">Copy public key</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_copied">Copied</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_fingerprint">Fingerprint: %1$s</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_linux_title">Linux</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_linux_text">Add the key line to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys of your user. Then allow shutdown without a password: run sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/wakedeck and add this line (replace youruser, and check the path with: which shutdown):\nyouruser ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/shutdown</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_windows_title">Windows</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_windows_text">Install the OpenSSH Server optional feature and start the sshd service. For an administrator account, put the key line in C:\\ProgramData\\ssh\\administrators_authorized_keys and restrict its permissions (only Administrators and SYSTEM). For a normal account use C:\\Users\\NAME\\.ssh\\authorized_keys.</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_regenerate">Create a new key</string>
    <string name="ssh_key_regenerate_warning">The current key stops working on every PC. You will have to add the new key again.</string>
